- Source files, drafts, version history, metadata for documents claimed confidential.
- Logs, server records, access logs (if relevant), and any evidence showing who accessed or exported files.
- Preserve original devices (phones, laptops) or at least make forensic copies.

Witness material
- Names and contact info for potential witnesses: employees, clients, childcare providers, third parties who saw relevant conduct.
- Any witness statements you can obtain now (short signed or emailed statements).

Protective or sensitive material
- A proposed list of documents you consider confidential or trade secret (helps draft a protective order).
- Any NDAs signed between the business and clients which demonstrate confidentiality practices.

