  - Would we be better served by an early neutral evaluation, private mediation, or waiting until after limited discovery?

Evidence checklist — what to gather and organize now
- Contractual documents
  - Signed NDA(s), amendments, related contracts, drafts, non-signed versions
  - Related corporate formation/ownership documents, operating agreements, buy-sell agreements

- Communications and ESI
  - Emails (client and business accounts) and relevant threads
  - Text messages, iMessages, Slack, WhatsApp, Signal, other chat logs
  - Calendars, meeting notes, call logs
  - Social media posts related to the dispute

- Business & financial records
  - Bank statements, invoices, accounting records, tax returns, payroll records
  - Client/customer lists, sales records showing loss or diversion of business
  - Evidence of revenue/profits before and after alleged disclosure

- Technical and access evidence
  - File system logs, access logs, server logs, cloud storage access histories, file metadata
  - Backups, Git/commit histories, document version histories
  - Screenshots or exports of files, including timestamps and metadata if possible

- Evidence of the alleged disclosure/use
  - Copies of the allegedly disclosed materials (webpages, product listings, investor materials)
